{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr534gig0ek","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM partial adoption repair no show root cause: masked wrapper swallows expect divergence","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: In the EWM agent, a partial-adopted program is a MaskedProgram that renders UNKNOWN over exactly the cells its inner source gets wrong. The live divergence check (env grids_match on expect grids) is UNKNOWN-aware and skips masked cells as wildcards. When the wrong cells are the object's MOVING cells (Run-10: wrong movement magnitude), the plan's masked expect grid is UNKNOWN over the whole moving region, so a real board divergence there is NEVER seen: _execute returns diverged=False, _handle_divergence/_repair never run, and the loop silently falls to reactive (the 14 divergences = reactive_turns, 0 repair_attempts). Fix: until the first live repair on a partial adoption, _execute reveals the unwrapped inner prediction ONLY on cells inner's step actually MOVES (inner_before != inner_after), keeping static masked cells as wildcards (Run-9 tolerance). Separately, the partial-adoption floor was measured whole-board (64x64 ~97% static background), so a wrong-magnitude model scored ~0.99 and cleared the 0.6 floor; the floor now scores CHANGED cells only (before != after per transition), where such a model scores ~0 and is refused. RunSummary gains changed_cells_accuracy at adoption time.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T15:25:10.936Z","vec":[-0.05349927768111229,-0.02161635272204876,0.055750563740730286,0.09465242922306061,0.10402381420135498,-0.06114495173096657,-0.0897916704416275,0.028334397822618484,-0.06078723073005676,0.017484154552221298,0.04486338794231415,-0.0753716304898262,0.004578830674290657,-0.03147447109222412,-0.03312471881508827,0.008049257099628448,-0.008455519564449787,-0.041276849806308746,-0.08928444236516953,0.0037624789401888847,-0.04201159253716469,0.020028335973620415,-0.02299063839018345,-0.01